  "result": "The `exp` field in a JWT is in **seconds** since Unix epoch, but `Date.now()` returns **milliseconds**. Your comparison is always false because `Date.now()` (~1.7 trillion) is always greater than `exp` (~1.7 billion).\n\n**Broken:**\n```js\nif (Date.now() > payload.exp) {\n  return res.status(401).json({ error: 'Token expired' });\n}\n```\n\n**Fixed:**\n```js\nif (Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000) > payload.exp) {\n  return res.status(401).json({ error: 'Token expired' });\n}\n```\n\nOr equivalently:\n```js\nif (Date.now() > payload.exp * 1000) {\n  return res.status(401).json({ error: 'Token expired' });\n}\n```\n\nIf you share the actual middleware file I can patch it directly.",
